# Package Manager: Yarn

This project uses **Yarn** exclusively. Never use `npm`, `pnpm`, or `bun` for any package operation.

## Commands

```bash
yarn install              # install dependencies
yarn add <pkg>            # add a dependency
yarn add -D <pkg>         # add a dev dependency
yarn remove <pkg>         # remove a dependency
yarn run <script>         # run a package.json script (yarn <script> shorthand works)
```

## Rules

- Only `yarn.lock` is committed. Never commit `package-lock.json`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`, or other lock files — delete them if found.
- Never delete or regenerate `yarn.lock` to "fix" an install issue; resolve the underlying conflict instead.
- `package.json` and `yarn.lock` are always committed together in the same commit.
- Prefer the latest stable version when adding dependencies; never pin arbitrary old versions.
- Use `yarn install --frozen-lockfile` in CI.
